(1. HOW TO APPLY AN EXCLUSION) Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(Exclusions must be matched to facts and read with exceptions and endorsements.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(EXC-1.1  Burden of explanation) Tj
T*
(   A rejection identifies the exact exclusion, relevant facts, evidence and causal) Tj
T*
(   connection. Keyword similarity alone is insufficient.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(EXC-1.2  Specific over general) Tj
T*
(   Use the most specific applicable clause. Do not combine unrelated exclusions to construct) Tj
T*
(   a broader denial.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(EXC-1.3  Exceptions and overrides) Tj
T*
(   Read every exception, benefit grant and endorsement before applying an exclusion. A) Tj
T*
(   covered carve-back controls within its stated scope.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(EXC-1.4  Diagnostic uncertainty) Tj
T*
(   Suspected, ruled-out and family-history conditions are not equivalent to a confirmed) Tj
T*
(   diagnosis.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
endstream
