(4. CONDITION-SPECIFIC INTERPRETATION) Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(Disease names alone do not decide coverage.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(EXC-4.1  HIV and infectious disease) Tj
T*
(   HIV or another infectious diagnosis is not listed as a blanket permanent exclusion in) Tj
T*
(   this demonstration plan. Apply active benefits, medical necessity, waiting periods and) Tj
T*
(   lawful terms.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(EXC-4.2  Parkinson disease and dementia) Tj
T*
(   Parkinson disease, dementia and Alzheimer disease are not blanket exclusions. Covered) Tj
T*
(   hospitalization is assessed under normal rules; custodial or long-term residential care) Tj
T*
(   may fall under EXC-2.2.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(EXC-4.3  Congenital conditions) Tj
T*
(   A congenital diagnosis is not automatically excluded. Review the benefit schedule,) Tj
T*
(   newborn cover, medical necessity and applicable requirements.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(EXC-4.4  Mental health and attempted self-harm) Tj
T*
(   Mental healthcare is a covered category under POL-5.4. Self-harm-related care requires) Tj
T*
(   sensitive clinical and legal review, not automatic keyword rejection.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(EXC-4.5  Pregnancy complications) Tj
T*
(   Pregnancy-related treatment is subject to maternity rules, but a condition unrelated to) Tj
T*
(   pregnancy must be assessed independently.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
endstream
